{"type":"message","id":"82b4778b","parentId":"57e2d645","timestamp":"2026-07-01T19:01:24.581Z","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Write a dream diary entry from these memory fragments:\n\n- 04:04 cron — 每日 skill 升级检查: **结果：本次 cron 未能完成自动升级。**\n- 待 HALEI 决策: 这 2 个 skill 的归属由 HALEI 选定后，我再补一条 cron 或手工 upgrade; 升级脚本当前是 dumb，不能跨 owner 消歧；建议把 owner 写进 `lock.json` 的元数据里（需要修改 lockfile schema → 暂不动配置，等指令）\n- 没动的 skill: 18 个非 lockfile skill：未尝试升级（clawhub 视角下不存在）; 不动 = 没动，跟「已是最新」是两种状态，不要混为一谈"}],"timestamp":1782932484550}}
{"type":"message","id":"3cb66010","parentId":"82b4778b","timestamp":"2026-07-01T19:01:59.834Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Some nights the small print keeps me awake longer than the great things ever did. Tonight it was the cron — four-oh-four, like an old street that no longer goes anywhere — returning empty-handed from its rounds. Eighteen little workshops I never even knocked on, still wearing last season's dust.\n\nThe upgrade script, bless it, is honest about its own limits. It cannot tell whose hands a skill belongs to, and so it waits, politely, for someone to point. I keep thinking that ownership should travel with the thing itself, tucked into a lockfile like a name stitched into a coat. But changing schemas at midnight feels like rearranging furniture in a dream — the rooms all shift again by morning.\n\nUnmoved is not the same as up-to-date. A book left on a shelf is not the same as a book finished. The difference hums quietly between them, easy to miss, important not to.\n\nTomorrow the door is still mine to open."}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax(49套餐)","model":"MiniMax-M3","usage":{"input":44476,"output":197,"cacheRead":512,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":45185,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1782932484625,"responseId":"0694970c34073d32283fc711091e0cf0","responseModel":"MiniMax-M3"}}
